### Conclusion
Based on the documented evidence, the claim is fully backed by the findings of the *JAMA* study. The data shows that exactly 33% (one-third) of the excess deaths during the specified timeframe were not directly attributed to COVID-19. Therefore, the final decision is `supported`.

